================ SUPPLEMENTARY PROBES (appended) ================
(3) EXACT FORMULA confirmed for all n=3..7:
    c3(T_G) = #{i<j<k : edges ij,jk present, ik absent}
            + #{i<j<k : edges ij,jk absent, ik present}
    i.e. #3-cycles = (induced-P3's whose endpoints are the OUTER labels
    i,k with the apex at the MIDDLE label j in G) + (same in complement).
    It is NOT total P3(G) or total P3(Gbar): the apex must be the middle label.

(5) MEANING of the order-existential split (verified all graphs n=3..6):
    'EXISTS a vertex order making T_G strong' <=> G nonempty AND noncomplete
      <=> tau in [1,n-2] <=> alcuin = tau+1 in [2, n-1].
    So the ONLY clean alcuin<->tournament link is the trivial degenerate one:
    alcuin=1 (empty G, transitive T, no order helps) and alcuin=n (complete G,
    transitive T). Strictly-between alcuin values are NOT distinguished.

    strong <=> Ham-cycle for T_G confirmed all n=3..7 (Moon/Camion).
